# ShiftWeave Full AWS Deployment Runbook

This document describes how to deploy the complete ShiftWeave project to AWS:

```text
React dashboard
+ Express backend
+ MCP Streamable HTTP server
+ SQLite workflow database
+ Epic adapter
+ optional Bedrock/Gemini adapter
+ Caddy HTTPS proxy
+ durable checkpoints
+ handoffs, tasks, conflicts, audit logs, and recovery
```

The authoritative target architecture for this runbook is:

```text
Judges / MCP clients / browser (Alexa+-style simulator)
                         |
                         | HTTPS 443
                         v
                 Elastic IP + DNS A record
                         |
                         v
        Account A: EC2 t4g.medium (us-west-2)
        ├── Caddy
        │   └── TLS, compression, reverse proxy,
        │       no buffering for /mcp
        ├── ShiftWeave application
        │   ├── Express + React production build
        │   ├── Public MCP server at /mcp
        │   ├── Workflow services + SQLite WAL
        │   ├── Alexa+-style simulator agent
        │   │   ├── STS AssumeRole to Account B
        │   │   └── MCPClientBridge to
        │   │       http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp
        │   └── No model calls inside MCP tool handlers
        └── Encrypted EBS gp3
            ├── SQLite database and WAL files
            └── local backup staging

        Account A supporting services
        ├── ECR: immutable ARM64 image
        ├── SSM Parameter Store: configuration and SecureString values
        ├── SSM Session Manager: host access without public SSH
        ├── CloudWatch: logs, metrics and alarms
        ├── EBS snapshots: volume recovery
        ├── S3: off-host SQLite backups
        └── AWS Budgets: Account A spend guardrail

        Account B supporting services
        ├── Bedrock runtime
        ├── tightly scoped cross-account inference role
        └── AWS Budget: Bedrock spend guardrail
```

