## 21. Configure SSM Parameter Store

The target architecture uses Systems Manager Parameter Store for runtime configuration and protected values in Account A.

Use a consistent path:

```text
/shiftweave/production/*
```

Use `SecureString` with a customer-managed KMS key for:

```text
/shiftweave/production/DEMO_PASSWORD
/shiftweave/production/MCP_AUTH_TOKEN
/shiftweave/production/EPIC_CLIENT_ID
/shiftweave/production/EPIC_KID
/shiftweave/production/EPIC_TOKEN_URL
/shiftweave/production/EPIC_FHIR_BASE_URL
/shiftweave/production/EPIC_TEST_PATIENT_IDS
/shiftweave/production/BEDROCK_ROLE_ARN
/shiftweave/production/BEDROCK_MODEL_ID
```

Non-secret values may use `String`, but keep the same path and access policy:

```text
/shiftweave/production/NODE_ENV
/shiftweave/production/HOST
/shiftweave/production/PORT
/shiftweave/production/PUBLIC_ORIGIN
/shiftweave/production/LLM_PROVIDER
/shiftweave/production/EPIC_READS_ENABLED
/shiftweave/production/EPIC_WRITES_ENABLED
```

The EC2 role must be allowed to call `ssm:GetParametersByPath` only for `/shiftweave/production`, plus `kms:Decrypt` only on the KMS key used by those parameters. Do not grant broad `ssm:*` or `kms:Decrypt` on all keys.

Parameter Store does not automatically inject values into Docker. Choose and document one verified mechanism:

1. A deployment script reads the parameters and writes a mode-600 `.env.deploy` file before `docker compose up`; or
2. The application startup code loads the parameter path before runtime configuration is evaluated.

Do not combine both mechanisms without defining precedence. Do not leave stale secrets in shell history or temporary files.

Use Secrets Manager instead of Parameter Store when the private key or another value needs managed rotation, binary secret handling, or a dedicated secret lifecycle. If Secrets Manager is selected, the same rule applies: the running application or deployment process must actually retrieve the secret.

