## 35B. Validate the ARM64 image before deployment

The target `t4g.medium` is ARM64. Validate the exact image that will run in Account A:

```powershell
docker buildx imagetools inspect `
  ACCOUNT_ID.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/shiftweave:TAG
```

The image manifest must include:

```text
linux/arm64
```

On an ARM64 test runtime, verify:

```bash
uname -m
docker run --rm IMAGE node --version
docker run --rm IMAGE node -e "const Database=require('better-sqlite3'); const db=new Database(':memory:'); console.log(db.prepare('SELECT 1 AS ok').get()); db.close()"
```

Expected architecture:

```text
aarch64
linux/arm64
{ ok: 1 }
```

If you cannot test ARM64 before deployment, use a multi-architecture image and treat the first EC2 launch as a compatibility validation gate. Do not silently fall back to an x86 image on `t4g.medium`.

The Windows development device can remain x86-64. Buildx cross-builds the ARM64 Linux image, but successful source compilation on Windows does not prove that the Linux ARM64 native `better-sqlite3` module works. The image, not the source checkout, is the deployment artifact that must be validated.

